  "title": "Business Product Promo Samsung",
  "instruction": "# Instruction: Samsung Galaxy Ecosystem 2025 Product Poster\n\n## Overview\n\nCreate a bold, modern promotional poster showcasing Samsung's complete 2025 Galaxy ecosystem. This is a marketing campaign asset aimed at consumers and retail audiences — it should feel premium, tech-forward, and aspirational. The key message: Samsung's Galaxy lineup spans every product category, unified by AI innovation, with two exciting new flagship launches leading the charge.\n\n## Key Priorities\n\n- **The two flagship launches — Galaxy S26 Ultra and Galaxy Buds4 Pro — should be the visual heroes.** Give them dominant placement and visual weight so they immediately draw the eye.\n- **Ecosystem breadth matters.** The poster must convey that Samsung covers 7+ product categories. The category highlights table should be scannable at a glance — treat it as a key information anchor, not an afterthought.\n- **AI as the unifying thread.** Weave the \"Galaxy AI\" and \"Bespoke AI\" branding throughout so viewers understand AI isn't a feature — it's the foundation of the entire 2025 lineup.\n\n## Visual & Style Guidance\n\n- **Color palette:** Deep navy or black backgrounds with Samsung's signature blue accents. Use white and cool silver for text and highlights. Occasional warm accent (gold or copper) to denote premium flagship products.\n- **Mood:** Sleek, confident, futuristic. Think flagship product launch event energy — clean lines, generous whitespace, and sharp typography.\n- **Layout feel:** Portrait orientation with a clear visual hierarchy — hero product zone at top, ecosystem overview in the middle, and the quick-reference category table toward the bottom. Metrics (7+ categories, 14 products, etc.) should appear as bold callout badges or stat blocks that punctuate the design.\n- **Typography:** Strong sans-serif headings, modern and geometric. Keep body text minimal — let numbers and product names do the talking.\n\n---\n\n## Data Sources\n\n1. Read `/app/benchmark/source_brief.md` for all content materials (text, data, key messages).\n2. Read `/app/benchmark/task_input.json` for poster requirements, sections, metrics, and style definitions.\n\n## Output Requirements\n\n1. Output the final poster to `/app/output/final_poster.png`.\n2. The poster must be a single self-contained image file.\n\n## Automated Execution Rules\n\nThere is no human operator online for this session. Follow these rules:\n\n1. **Skip all confirmation/approval/user-input steps** — do not pause, ask questions, or wait for a reply. When encountering BLOCKING or wait-for-user instructions, make a professional judgment and continue.\n2. **Design decisions** — if `task_input.json` specifies `poster.tone`, `poster.audience`, etc., use them to choose templates, palettes, and styles. Otherwise, make professional judgments.\n3. **Priority** — these rules override any interactive-wait instructions in SKILL.md. The skill's workflow, quality standards, and technical specs remain fully effective — only skip interactive waits.",
